In the middle of the night, someone shouted: "Here is the groom! Come to welcome him!"
Then all the little brides woke up and put their lamps ready.
The ignorant said to the wise, "Give us some of your oil. For our lamps are burning."
"No," they replied. "There may not be enough for all of us. Instead, go to those who sell the oil. Buy some for yourselves."
So they went to buy the oil. But while they were on their way, the bridegroom arrived. So the bride went in with him, along with the maids who were ready for the wedding feast. Then the door was locked.
