Then Jesus went with his disciples to a place called Gethsemani. He said to them, "Sit here while I go over there and pray."
Peter took John and James, the sons of Zebedee, along with him. He began to feel sorrowful and distressed.
Then he said to them, "My soul is very sorrowful. I feel that I am about to die. Stay here. Watch with me."
He went a little way; then fell on his face to the ground. He prayed, "My Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me; nevertheless, not my will, but thine, be done."
Then he came back to his disciples and found them sleeping. "Could you men not watch with me for one hour?" Peter asked.
Look and pray. Then you will not fall into temptation when you are tempted. The spirit is willing. But the flesh is weak.
Jesus went out again. He prayed, saying, "My Father, if it is possible, let this cup pass from me; yet not as I will, but as you will."
Then he went back. He found them sleeping again. They couldn't keep their eyes open.
So he left them and departed once more. He prayed the same supplication for the third time.
Then he went back to the disciples. He said to them, "Are you still sleeping and taking your rest? Look! The hour is near. The Son of Man is about to be handed over to sinners."
